course: dictionary
lesson: 4894
title: The Roman numeral ii
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: ii is a Roman numeral. It means 2. You can write it in small letters, ii, or in capitals, II. The Romans used numbers like this long ago, and we still see them today on clocks, in books and in names.
explain: In a list or a book, (ii) numbers a section, just like (i) is the first and (iii) is the third. «Part ii» means the second part. «Question (ii)» means the second question. Look for the brackets or the word part before you read it as a number.
explain: After a name, II means "the second". «Henry II» is read as "Henry the Second", and «Queen Elizabeth II» is read as "Elizabeth the Second". The numbers go I = 1, II = 2, III = 3, IV = 4, V = 5, so count along to check.
fact: ii is a Roman numeral, and it means 2.
fact: ii and II mean the same thing; capital letters are often used in names.
fact: «Mehmed II» captured Constantinople in 1453, ending the Byzantine Empire.
fact: «Philip II» of Spain gave the Philippines their name, and Spain ruled them from 1565 to 1898.
fact: «Blue Planet II» is a nature film that made many people think about plastic in the sea.
exercise: «Part ii» of the book starts on page ten. What does ii mean? | The last part | The third part | The first part | *The second part
exercise: In the list (i) Dogs, (ii) Cats, what does (ii) show? | Four items | *The second item | A question about cats | The first item
exercise: «Henry II» is read as Henry the Second. How do you read «Queen Elizabeth II»? | *Elizabeth the Second | Elizabeth the Third | Elizabeth the Two | Elizabeth the First
test: In the Roman numeral II, what number is it? | Twelve | Three | One | *Two
test: In «Philip II», what does II mean? | Ten | *The second | The first | The king's favourite
exam: In «Mehmed II captured Constantinople in 1453», what does II mean? | The first | Two hundred | Ten | *The second
